WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.803
Open Computer is an open, self-hostable computer-use agent.

2
00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:07.225
You give it a goal in plain words.

3
00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:09.899
The goal becomes a plan of steps.

4
00:00:09.899 --> 00:00:16.025
Each step is routed to a model that fits it, and shows its own state, its model and its cost.

5
00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:22.434
Every step runs in its own disposable sandbox, with outbound traffic denied by default.

6
00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:27.800
Every model call goes through a router that picks the cheapest model that fits.

7
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.700
Anything sensitive stops and waits.

8
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:37.350
Here, a step that would send invoice figures to a cloud model is held until a person approves it.

9
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:43.650
When the steps finish, the run shows what each one did, and what it cost against a budget cap.

10
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.072
Today it is an early runtime.

11
00:00:46.072 --> 00:00:52.234
The safety pieces are built, but a full run from goal to finished artifact is not proven yet.

12
00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:57.800
Version one is planned as a desktop app, plus a core in your own Cloudflare account.
